AB  - The timely and accurate identification of cocoa pod maturity is a critical determinant of crop yield and quality; however, traditional manual inspection is inefficient and inconsistent. Deep learning offers a non-destructive solution, yet the efficacy of Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) is strictly limited by suboptimal hyperparameter configurations. To address this, this study uses Bayesian Optimization to automate the hyperparameter search for a DenseNet-201 backbone, targeting optimal classification accuracy on the CocoaMFDB dataset. The proposed framework successfully identified a streamlined architecture that achieved a classification accuracy of 99.20%, significantly surpassing the 80.00% accuracy of the baseline model. Furthermore, comparative analysis revealed that the optimized DenseNet-201 outperformed standard pre-trained networks such as MobileNetV2, ResNet-50, and VGG16. These results validate Bayesian Optimization as a powerful tool for reducing computational overhead while maximizing diagnostic precision in precision agriculture.
