AB  - This dataset contains 4,753 field images of cocoa (Theobroma cacao) leaves from smallholder farms in Berau Regency, East Kalimantan, Indonesia. The leaves are annotated with 6,021 bounding boxes in 12 classes: healthy leaf; four diseases: Phytophthora leaf blight, vascular streak dieback, horse-tail blight and anthracnose; three types of insect damage: leaf beetle, looper caterpillar and Helopeltis; four macronutrient deficiencies: N, P, K and Mg. The images were taken with smartphones under natural light, so they include real backgrounds such as soil, stems, other leaves and hands. Blurred images were removed. Each leaf was labelled from its visible symptoms, and a portable chlorophyll meter was used as supporting evidence for the nutrient-deficiency classes. The labels were verified in two rounds by an agronomist. Disagreements were resolved by consensus, and ambiguous images were excluded. Number of annotations per class: healthy 1,719; Phytophthora leaf blight 209; vascular streak dieback 458; horse-tail blight 531; anthracnose 559; leaf beetle 462; looper caterpillar 282; Helopeltis 408; N deficiency 313; P deficiency 374; K deficiency 373; Mg deficiency 333. Files: images in train/valid/test folders, annotations in COCO JSON format (_annotations.coco.json) which lists every leaf box with its class, split, and image name. The dataset can be used for leaf disorder classification, leaf detection and explainable AI studies in precision agriculture. Note: the split was made per image. Some photos taken in the same burst appear in different splits. For a strict evaluation, we recommend grouping images by capture session.
