AB  - Cocoa fruit is a type of plantation commodity with high economic value. With increasing production and market demand, various forms of technology are needed to support the acceleration of cocoa production and post-production. Cocoa farmers sort and determine the ripeness of cocoa fruit based on estimates from farmers. This causes post-harvest production handling to be less effective and efficient. The ripeness detection and sorting system for cocoa fruit is an innovation that can help detect ripeness and sort cocoa fruit automatically. This system is designed using the TCS3200 sensor which can read the RGB value of the skin color of the cocoa fruit, Arduino Uno, and a servo motor as a sorter for the cocoa fruit. The system built produces a sorting accuracy of 70%.
